# Jak 1 hands against the world (item 25): to play on Geyser Rock (as jak1_down_out.sim), the head turned 40 degrees
# right toward the cliff (the stick moves him where the head looks; straight ahead the path runs on to the beach), a
# run at it until it stops him, then the right hand pushed 30 and 60 cm on along the look into the rock, then the left.
# Look for "[vr-body] the right hand meets the world" in run.log; w-reach and w-push show the hand held at the rock.
# Then the right hand pushed 2.2 m down into the ground (w-floor), a slow walk on to the rock (w-close) and the reach
# again (w-wall).
# (The sim's hand offsets are not turned with the head: 0.6 along a look 40 degrees right is x 0.38, z -0.46.)
2400 menu 1
2406 menu 0
2700 a 1
2706 a 0
3000 a 1
3006 a 0
3420 y 1
3426 y 0
4150 head_yaw -40
4200 shot w-turned
4200 left_y 1
4560 left_y 0
4620 shot w-near
4630 rh_y 0.25
4630 rh_x 0.19
4630 rh_z -0.23
4690 shot w-reach
4700 rh_x 0.38
4700 rh_z -0.46
4760 shot w-push
4770 rh_y 0
4770 rh_x 0
4770 rh_z 0
4780 lh_y 0.25
4780 lh_x 0.38
4780 lh_z -0.46
4840 shot w-left
4850 lh_y 0
4850 lh_x 0
4850 lh_z 0
4860 rh_y -2.2
4920 shot w-floor
4930 rh_y 0
4940 left_y 0.4
5100 left_y 0
5110 shot w-close
5120 rh_y 0.25
5120 rh_x 0.38
5120 rh_z -0.46
5180 shot w-wall
5190 rh_y 0
5190 rh_x 0
5190 rh_z 0
5200 quit 0
